>
> Okay, just for fun, what would you prefer?
> As an orcish ranger, having a:
> 50/50 chance of Stormbringer or Grimtooth, or a
> 1 in 4 chance each of Sunsword, Demonbane, Grayswandir, or
> Snickersnee?

Stormbringer, Greyswandir and Snickersnee are ascendable
super artifacts.  So in both cases there's a 50/50 chance of
getting an ascendable super artifact.  There are a minority of
players who think of Stormbringer as a super artifact and I am
in that minority.

On the one hand, Sunsword and Demonbane are long swords
that unrestrict a very good weapons slot, and a skilled player
will be able to ascend with them.  On the other hand both are
nearly guaranteed in an endurance game as they are given to
5% of Angels and 100% of Archons.  Stay in the game long
enough to kill at least two randomly generated Archons and
you get them.  Since so many artifacts are long swords getting
one of the unligned ones is fairly likely for a player who wants
lots of artifacts.

In comparison Grimtooth is a very good dagger for a class
that gets expert in dagger and it's not generated anywhere in
the game before Astral except as gifts or wishes or bones.  A
chaotic player can get Sunsword and/or Demonbane but a
lawful player can't get Grimtooth.

To me the choise starts out very slightly in favor of the
chaotic choices before taking protection into account.  While
the lawful artifacts are better than the chaotic ones, as an
orc your first one won't be the elvish Orcrist or Sting and that
basically eliminates the advantage of lawful artifacts.  As a
non-orc you can always create Sting and Orcrist first to bias
your odds - It may effect the second gift but it has no effect on
the first one.

